WEBVTT

00:01:45.260 --> 00:01:47.050
The R is chasing us.

00:01:48.380 --> 00:01:49.920
That's kind of dangerous.

00:01:50.180 --> 00:01:51.010
Are you ok?

00:01:51.440 --> 00:01:53.670
They think they can just smoke me?

00:01:53.900 --> 00:01:56.210
This baby's got 450 horsepower.

00:01:57.710 --> 00:01:59.210
<i>So, you're coming, R?</i>

00:01:59.990 --> 00:02:03.220
<i>Indeed, it's a good car, fast and easy to ride.</i>

00:02:03.790 --> 00:02:06.420
<i>But are you sure you got it under control, kid?</i>

00:02:07.940 --> 00:02:09.940
I'll take 'em both from the left!

00:02:10.500 --> 00:02:11.730
First is the Testa'!

00:02:13.580 --> 00:02:14.890
And next, the Z!

00:02:17.480 --> 00:02:18.660
How was that?!

00:02:21.580 --> 00:02:22.780
See ya later!

00:02:22.780 --> 00:02:23.560
Hey!

00:02:56.150 --> 00:02:57.020
<i>The Tuner from Hell</i>

00:02:57.020 --> 00:02:59.320
<i>Accident on the Wangan-sen.</i>

00:02:59.320 --> 00:03:01.620
<i>Traffic is already backed up 2km.</i>

00:03:01.930 --> 00:03:06.000
<i>Only one car in the accident, but he
says he was driving with others.</i>

00:03:06.660 --> 00:03:09.810
<i>Put up checkpoints at the Yokohama-sen interchange.</i>

00:03:28.020 --> 00:03:29.140
The Tohmei Freeway?

00:03:29.140 --> 00:03:30.670
Yeah, I know.

00:03:31.140 --> 00:03:36.090
Because of that accident, we'll have
to stay off the Wangan for a while.

00:03:38.100 --> 00:03:41.640
Still, he's an amazing driver.

00:03:42.350 --> 00:03:45.270
He just keeps going, eh?

00:03:59.120 --> 00:04:00.010
Dammit.

00:04:00.340 --> 00:04:01.960
How could this happen at a time like this?

00:04:02.290 --> 00:04:03.710
What's the matter?

00:04:05.150 --> 00:04:07.470
The car behind you is slowing down.

00:04:19.680 --> 00:04:21.040
My belt snapped.

00:04:21.040 --> 00:04:22.010
Your belt?

00:04:23.150 --> 00:04:24.060
Dammit.

00:04:24.600 --> 00:04:25.620
What are you gonna do?

00:04:25.620 --> 00:04:27.170
Call it a night?

00:04:32.110 --> 00:04:34.280
You're wearing pants, so I don't
suppose you're wearing those...

00:04:35.520 --> 00:04:37.500
Wearing... what?

00:04:40.450 --> 00:04:44.020
That stopped car... looks like a couple's inside.

00:04:44.370 --> 00:04:46.680
W-Wait, Ishida-sensei... what are you doing?

00:04:49.430 --> 00:04:51.420
Sorry to interrupt...

00:04:52.170 --> 00:04:53.690
W-Who the hell are you!?

00:04:53.890 --> 00:04:56.490
I'm sorry but I have a favor to ask.

00:04:57.410 --> 00:05:02.220
Do you think I could buy the pantyhose she's wearing?

00:05:11.630 --> 00:05:12.490
Sensei...

00:05:13.330 --> 00:05:15.700
Can you wait at that restaurant for a while?

00:05:16.760 --> 00:05:18.010
What are you going to do?

00:05:18.520 --> 00:05:19.090
Me?

00:05:20.020 --> 00:05:22.000
I'm gonna go a little farther north.

00:05:22.870 --> 00:05:25.000
Hakone at night sounds good.

00:05:25.420 --> 00:05:26.020
I'll tag along.

00:05:26.720 --> 00:05:27.350
Sure, but...

00:05:28.410 --> 00:05:30.320
There's so many curves... not interesting at all.

00:05:36.440 --> 00:05:37.260
Alright.

00:05:37.720 --> 00:05:42.250
Pantyhose are pretty tough, so they can
make a nice substitute for a belt.

00:05:42.670 --> 00:05:45.220
I wouldn't expect anything less from you.

00:05:45.610 --> 00:05:46.890
So, what now?

00:05:47.310 --> 00:05:48.910
I'll go back to Tokyo for now.

00:05:50.160 --> 00:05:51.280
Don't worry.

00:05:52.120 --> 00:05:57.250
No matter where he is right now, he'll
come back to Wangan by dawn.

00:06:10.280 --> 00:06:13.760
<i>I have no sense of speed or reality right in front of me.</i>

00:06:15.020 --> 00:06:19.640
<i>It's like I'm watching a movie or something.</i>

00:06:23.540 --> 00:06:27.020
Is this what it means to "drive"?

00:06:36.300 --> 00:06:37.150
Wow!

00:06:37.450 --> 00:06:39.040
The stars are amazing!

00:06:41.990 --> 00:06:43.410
I'm glad I came.

00:06:44.730 --> 00:06:47.180
This is a lot better than having coffee by myself.

00:06:49.000 --> 00:06:50.330
You're a good driver.

00:06:50.890 --> 00:06:54.800
Seems like you can control this "devil"
as if it were your own hands.

00:06:55.410 --> 00:06:58.820
Is this from practice? Or talent?

00:06:59.160 --> 00:07:01.810
I'm not sure about that.

00:07:09.390 --> 00:07:10.120
What's the matter?

00:07:10.990 --> 00:07:11.860
I'm just...

00:07:13.170 --> 00:07:15.620
a little worried right now.

00:07:20.280 --> 00:07:26.000
<i>Here's the traffic news: the accident
has been cleared on the Wangan-sen.</i>

00:07:26.300 --> 00:07:29.790
<i>Right now, the flow is improving both
northbound and southbound.</i>

00:07:30.080 --> 00:07:30.970
What time is it?

00:07:31.310 --> 00:07:32.500
Just past 4:00.

00:07:32.800 --> 00:07:34.300
It'll get bright pretty soon.

00:07:41.910 --> 00:07:42.810
He's here.

00:07:48.760 --> 00:07:50.330
That car again?

00:08:17.010 --> 00:08:20.340
You said you were worried earlier... why?

00:08:21.520 --> 00:08:22.310
This car...

00:08:24.670 --> 00:08:30.760
It was born to drive but I just felt
like it's starting to resent it.

00:08:32.220 --> 00:08:35.830
As if... it's trying to kill itself.

00:08:36.800 --> 00:08:41.020
I'm sure this is how it denied many owners.

00:08:42.150 --> 00:08:45.460
Being born to drive, yet resenting it.

00:08:46.440 --> 00:08:47.620
But...

00:08:48.030 --> 00:08:49.500
I won't let it.

00:09:09.480 --> 00:09:10.810
No good after all?

00:09:14.170 --> 00:09:15.320
<i>He can't catch up.</i>

00:09:16.010 --> 00:09:19.500
<i>The Devil Z... is disappearing into the darkness.</i>

00:09:24.530 --> 00:09:28.580
<i>Today, I want to take a good look at this kid...</i>

00:09:29.300 --> 00:09:36.180
<i>Who has gotten into numerous accidents and been
called the devil but still insists on driving this car.</i>

00:09:36.680 --> 00:09:41.090
<i>As if he was searching for something on Wangan.</i>

00:09:45.730 --> 00:09:47.720
Ok, that's a wrap!

00:09:50.310 --> 00:09:51.020
Eh!?

00:09:51.470 --> 00:09:53.980
You found out who built the Devil Z?

00:09:57.020 --> 00:09:59.050
I didn't see it with my own eyes,

00:09:59.370 --> 00:10:06.250
but based on your story, I'm pretty sure
the Z you saw was in fact the Devil Z.

00:10:06.630 --> 00:10:09.020
You sure have connections.

00:10:09.020 --> 00:10:10.570
You found out so fast.

00:10:11.900 --> 00:10:13.050
Well, I guess...

00:10:14.840 --> 00:10:15.960
It was a coincidence.

00:10:16.410 --> 00:10:18.760
I happened to know him a long time ago.

00:10:19.140 --> 00:10:20.000
Know him?

00:10:20.600 --> 00:10:21.560
Oh, right.

00:10:21.560 --> 00:10:23.700
You used to be a racing mechanic, right?

00:10:23.700 --> 00:10:24.740
So from back then?

00:10:25.080 --> 00:10:28.290
Reina-chan, promise me one thing.

00:10:28.290 --> 00:10:28.960
What?

00:10:29.440 --> 00:10:33.570
When we meet this guy, you won't ask him to tune your R.

00:10:35.690 --> 00:10:36.760
Promise me.

00:10:38.660 --> 00:10:41.570
Is that your pride speaking for you?

00:10:42.000 --> 00:10:44.580
That you put your hands on this R?

00:10:45.010 --> 00:10:46.160
It's not like that.

00:10:46.660 --> 00:10:50.840
I cannot let this R turn into something dangerous.

00:10:51.240 --> 00:10:52.250
Dangerous?

00:10:52.460 --> 00:10:53.000
Yeah.

00:10:53.430 --> 00:10:55.430
The cars he builds are dangerous.

00:10:56.270 --> 00:11:00.890
Enough to get the name, "The Tuner from Hell".

00:11:01.200 --> 00:11:02.730
The tuner from Hell?

00:11:10.390 --> 00:11:10.940
Eh?

00:11:11.400 --> 00:11:12.230
Here?

00:11:12.470 --> 00:11:13.360
Yeah.

00:11:18.200 --> 00:11:19.700
A bicycle shop?

00:11:20.820 --> 00:11:22.750
Is he really here?

00:11:22.750 --> 00:11:24.670
I heard it from an old friend...

00:11:25.120 --> 00:11:26.350
There's no doubt.

00:11:29.720 --> 00:11:31.000
Excuse me!

00:11:44.810 --> 00:11:46.500
Who are you?

00:11:49.000 --> 00:11:50.950
<i>Ever since, he's been coming to school...</i>

00:11:51.300 --> 00:11:53.690
<i>So as his homeroom teacher, I'm relieved.</i>

00:11:56.680 --> 00:11:59.920
<i>But I guess I need to keep my eyes on him.</i>

00:12:01.400 --> 00:12:04.770
I have no idea what you're talking about.

00:12:05.130 --> 00:12:08.950
We did our research... about a car known as the Devil Z.

00:12:09.640 --> 00:12:12.000
And that you built it.

00:12:13.490 --> 00:12:14.660
We just wanna hear your story.

00:12:15.440 --> 00:12:18.430
She's really interested in that Z.

00:12:18.430 --> 00:12:21.070
I don't know any car like that.

00:12:21.750 --> 00:12:23.370
Uncle Kitami!

00:12:23.810 --> 00:12:25.170
Hey, what's up?

00:12:25.170 --> 00:12:26.660
Our muffler came off.

00:12:26.950 --> 00:12:27.890
Can you put it on for us?

00:12:28.310 --> 00:12:29.410
Moron...

00:12:29.800 --> 00:12:31.710
I'll loan you the tools, so do it yourself.

00:12:33.240 --> 00:12:35.150
I'm sorry but can you leave?

00:12:35.640 --> 00:12:37.420
I'm pretty busy.

00:12:37.420 --> 00:12:38.030
But...!

00:12:39.180 --> 00:12:42.280
I've put together over 1000 engines.

00:12:42.980 --> 00:12:44.520
How can I remember every single one?

00:12:50.990 --> 00:12:54.760
He was in denial but there's no mistake...

00:12:55.150 --> 00:12:56.530
He made that Z.

00:13:01.170 --> 00:13:03.000
<i>Haven't heard that in a while.</i>

00:13:09.010 --> 00:13:11.200
<i>The Devil Z...</i>

00:13:22.490 --> 00:13:26.810
I first met Kitami on a circuit in Fuji, 20 years ago.

00:13:27.590 --> 00:13:30.820
I was a race mechanic back then.

00:13:31.000 --> 00:13:33.140
I was the best private tuner.

00:13:34.540 --> 00:13:40.010
Our cars were fast and were able to stand
up against the invincible rotary engines.

00:13:41.160 --> 00:13:48.660
But one day, we had the pole position taken
during the prelims by a private Z.

00:13:50.020 --> 00:13:55.850
That Z was frighteningly fast and Kitami
was the mechanic and driver.

00:13:55.850 --> 00:13:58.400
But on that day it rained.

00:13:59.530 --> 00:14:02.560
The Z's overwhelming power backfired in the rain...

00:14:03.020 --> 00:14:04.370
and retired early.

00:14:05.890 --> 00:14:11.160
One month after the race, Kitami
got into an accident with that Z.

00:14:11.980 --> 00:14:16.250
It seems Kitami put a plate on that car and drove it around.

00:14:16.850 --> 00:14:18.130
It was on the Tohmei Freeway.

00:14:18.680 --> 00:14:20.810
I heard it was a pretty bad accident.

00:14:22.620 --> 00:14:23.310
But...

00:14:23.810 --> 00:14:25.900
About two years after that accident,

00:14:26.340 --> 00:14:27.880
Kitami returned.

00:14:29.340 --> 00:14:31.800
In the middle of the night they raced from Yohga to Gotenba...

00:14:31.800 --> 00:14:33.980
It was known as the Tohmei race.

00:14:34.380 --> 00:14:38.090
He tuned the fastest machines there.

00:14:39.780 --> 00:14:41.440
Then, soon after that...

00:14:42.080 --> 00:14:47.490
a driver sustained serious injuries
driving one of KItami's machines.

00:14:49.110 --> 00:14:52.860
Ever since then, there were numerous accidents with his cars.

00:14:52.860 --> 00:14:54.210
Why so many?

00:14:54.680 --> 00:15:00.750
The answer is simple: no one could
control the machines he made.

00:15:02.840 --> 00:15:06.440
That's how he became known as "The Tuner from Hell".

00:15:06.900 --> 00:15:10.470
Of course, less people asked him to tune their cars.

00:15:10.970 --> 00:15:13.240
And the rumors died down.

00:15:13.500 --> 00:15:14.380
I see.

00:15:14.720 --> 00:15:16.730
That's why you said he was dangerous.

00:15:17.190 --> 00:15:20.260
He builds machines that no one can drive?

00:15:21.020 --> 00:15:22.750
The tuner from Hell...

00:15:35.900 --> 00:15:36.710
It's no good.

00:15:37.120 --> 00:15:39.000
It always dips around 5,000.

00:15:39.570 --> 00:15:41.890
It's pretty smooth higher up, though.

00:15:45.490 --> 00:15:47.830
Don't be so down, Akio...

00:15:48.230 --> 00:15:52.030
Bottom line is, this car's base is from decades ago...

00:15:52.360 --> 00:15:55.350
And if it can still run this well, I think it's fine.

00:15:55.680 --> 00:15:58.170
Besides, this is a good opportunity,

00:15:58.170 --> 00:16:03.360
you could match your pace with this old lady.

00:16:05.000 --> 00:16:07.560
So that's why it's been down lately?

00:16:09.050 --> 00:16:11.730
Maybe it didn't want to run anymore...

00:16:13.000 --> 00:16:17.930
Maybe it was telling me it only wanted
to run in its prime condition.

00:16:17.930 --> 00:16:19.620
Hey, hey... wait a second, Akio.

00:16:20.530 --> 00:16:24.000
Listen, cars are just machines.

00:16:24.000 --> 00:16:26.630
Nothing more and nothing less.

00:16:28.660 --> 00:16:30.620
I know that, Kou-chan.

00:16:46.020 --> 00:16:46.690
Here.

00:16:47.170 --> 00:16:48.020
Eh? Here?

00:16:52.580 --> 00:16:54.280
Thanks for this afternoon.

00:16:57.340 --> 00:16:58.260
Umm....

00:17:01.120 --> 00:17:04.280
I forgot to mention,

00:17:04.670 --> 00:17:06.420
did you know the Z is still running right now?

00:17:08.360 --> 00:17:11.800
It's out there, Kitami-san... the Devil Z.

00:17:12.770 --> 00:17:14.520
I told you, I know nothing.

00:17:15.010 --> 00:17:17.410
It's running... on Wangan!

00:17:19.800 --> 00:17:20.790
Wangan, eh?

00:17:21.750 --> 00:17:23.240
That doesn't matter to me.

00:17:23.770 --> 00:17:25.980
Why are you telling me this, missy?

00:17:27.150 --> 00:17:29.650
Because it's the car you built.

00:17:29.650 --> 00:17:34.000
That S30Z is still the devil it used to be and it's out there!

00:17:41.450 --> 00:17:43.330
Still a devil...?

00:17:43.330 --> 00:17:48.280
There's someone out there driving
the devil no one could control.

00:17:50.000 --> 00:17:51.490
It's true, Kitami-san.

00:17:51.830 --> 00:17:54.330
That speed is nothing short of the devil himself.

00:17:54.720 --> 00:17:57.340
Do you want to see it with your own eyes?

00:18:07.010 --> 00:18:08.170
I see.

00:18:08.170 --> 00:18:10.030
It's a nice road, just like the rumors say.

00:18:10.030 --> 00:18:12.300
Eh? You've never driven on Wangan before?

00:18:12.570 --> 00:18:13.030
No.

00:18:14.460 --> 00:18:18.110
With a road like this, cruising at 300 isn't impossible.

00:18:20.820 --> 00:18:22.880
You're not bad, kid.

00:18:23.770 --> 00:18:26.580
I'll make a U-turn at Ooi and get back on Kanjo-sen.

00:18:26.580 --> 00:18:29.080
Reina, don't go too fast on Kanjo, alright?

00:18:29.080 --> 00:18:30.630
I know.

00:18:41.120 --> 00:18:43.880
Did Yamamoto built this R for you?

00:18:43.880 --> 00:18:44.710
Yes.

00:18:45.000 --> 00:18:47.730
Right now, the boost is 1.2 and I have about 500hp.

00:18:49.120 --> 00:18:50.680
That's his style.

00:18:51.010 --> 00:18:53.400
Easy to drive, powerful and sturdy.

00:18:53.850 --> 00:18:55.080
It's a nice car.

00:18:55.440 --> 00:18:57.900
Yeah, a nice car indeed.

00:18:58.250 --> 00:19:04.420
But in this world there are some dangerous cars
out there and they're a lot more fun, missy.

00:19:07.880 --> 00:19:11.210
<i>It's true, there was something attractive
about the cars that Kitami built.</i>

00:19:11.550 --> 00:19:14.620
<i>Anyone with the need for speed would understand.</i>

00:19:15.010 --> 00:19:17.650
<i>A common fascination that they share.</i>

00:19:18.710 --> 00:19:22.510
<i>But at the same time, it's a very dangerous car.</i>

00:19:23.590 --> 00:19:27.020
<i>For some people, speeding works better than drugs.</i>

00:19:27.450 --> 00:19:32.230
<i>And the cars that Kitami builds, attract those kinds of guys.</i>

00:19:33.220 --> 00:19:36.720
<i>Despite the fact that the first accident seriously injured a man,</i>

00:19:37.600 --> 00:19:42.230
<i>the Tohmei racers were obsessed with Kitami's cars.</i>

00:19:43.020 --> 00:19:46.910
<i>Domestic, imported, L-Types to rotaries...</i>

00:19:47.390 --> 00:19:51.640
<i>2TGkai-turbo, Kitami tuned any engine.</i>

00:19:58.540 --> 00:20:00.250
Ishida-sensei, the car behind us.

00:20:07.430 --> 00:20:10.260
<i>Maybe we'll just have to overhaul, Kou-chan.</i>

00:20:10.640 --> 00:20:16.320
<i>But I'm not sure if there's anyone who can take
apart this engine and put it back together.</i>

00:20:17.000 --> 00:20:19.000
<i>I know I can't, Akio</i>

00:20:22.020 --> 00:20:23.640
<i>If I knew the guy who tuned it...</i>

00:20:31.350 --> 00:20:32.750
<i>She's getting on Wangan-sen.</i>

00:20:33.590 --> 00:20:35.000
<i>It must be her R.</i>

00:20:46.950 --> 00:20:47.630
He's coming...

00:20:47.630 --> 00:20:48.810
at an unbelievable speed.

00:20:51.910 --> 00:20:53.340
<i>There's no doubt.</i>

00:20:56.570 --> 00:20:57.360
He's here!

00:20:59.540 --> 00:21:01.320
<i>The Devil Z.</i>

00:21:03.000 --> 00:21:05.860
<i>It was alive...</i>

00:21:10.010 --> 00:21:16.410
<i>The cars Kitami builds make you crave for more...</i>

00:21:22.210 --> 00:21:26.090
<i>At the same time, no one could truly drive his machines.</i>

00:21:27.940 --> 00:21:30.620
<i>The Tohmei races kept causing accidents,</i>

00:21:30.940 --> 00:21:34.660
<i>and after a while, people stopped coming to Kitami.</i>

00:21:35.670 --> 00:21:37.320
<i>Machines that were too dangerous...</i>

00:21:38.750 --> 00:21:41.820
<i>He's really the tuner from Hell, Kitami Jun.</i>

00:21:43.130 --> 00:21:48.490
<i>Soon after, many lighter tuners appeared and competed
with him... and he lost more customers.</i>

00:21:48.800 --> 00:21:50.950
<i>In the end he was left with only debts to pay.</i>

00:21:52.090 --> 00:21:55.740
<i>But one day, he built a car.</i>

00:21:56.570 --> 00:21:58.810
<i>The car he loved the most.</i>

00:22:00.460 --> 00:22:05.140
<i>Kitami put everything into that car... L28 Twin Turbo.</i>

00:22:09.590 --> 00:22:10.850
Z...

00:22:11.660 --> 00:22:13.150
And the next year,

00:22:13.150 --> 00:22:16.560
<i>his shop went bankrupt and no one heard from him.</i>

00:22:22.620 --> 00:22:23.990
I won't let you get away.

00:22:32.990 --> 00:22:33.700
He's fast!

00:22:33.980 --> 00:22:35.250
Can you keep up, Reina?

00:22:50.140 --> 00:22:51.020
I can't...

00:22:51.340 --> 00:22:52.720
I can't keep up.

00:22:53.580 --> 00:22:54.970
It's no good.

00:22:55.560 --> 00:22:57.720
The way it is right now...

00:23:01.340 --> 00:23:03.720
If it keeps running the way it is right now,

00:23:04.250 --> 00:23:05.690
that Z will...

00:23:05.920 --> 00:23:07.300
definitely...

00:23:07.630 --> 00:23:08.870
die.
